  <!-- ================================================================
       ABOUT
       ================================================================ -->
  <section class="section about-section" id="about">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-text">
          <span class="section-label">About</span>
          <h2 class="section-heading">A city that shaped empires,<br />now shaping code</h2>
          <p><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Pune">पुणे</span> was the seat of <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj — founder of the Maratha Empire">छत्रपती शिवाजी महाराज</span> and the <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Peshwa — prime ministers of the Maratha Empire">पेशवे</span> who built one of the largest empires in Indian history. Today it is India's fastest-growing tech city and its most celebrated education hub — the <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Oxford of the East">पूर्वेचे ऑक्सफर्ड</span>.</p>
          <p>Deccan Queen on Rails is a community-first Rails conference rooted in that same spirit — bold thinking, deep craft, and warmth for everyone at the table. We bring Rails developers from across India together and invite voices from the global community to join the conversation.</p>
          <p>Expect honest talks, hallway conversations that shift your thinking — and a city that will make you want to stay longer than planned.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-callout">
          <div class="callout-card card">
            <div class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">🚂</div>
            <h4>The real Deccan Queen</h4>
            <p>The historic Deccan Queen express has run Pune ↔ Mumbai daily since 1930 — India's first superfast train and a source of enduring <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Pune pride">पुण्याभिमान</span>. Come for the conference. Arrive by train.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="callout-card card" style="margin-top:1rem">
            <div class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">💎</div>
            <h4>Community-first, always</h4>
            <p>No corporate bloat. A single track where everyone watches the same talks. Lunch together. <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="tea">चहा</span> together. Ideas shared freely.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pune at a Glance -->
      <div class="pune-glance" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">
        <div class="pune-glance-item">
          <span class="pg-emoji">⚔️</span>
          <strong><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Shivaji Maharaj's Pune">शिवाजी महाराजांची पुणे</span></strong>
          <p><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj">छत्रपती शिवाजी महाराज</span> was born near Pune and launched the Maratha Empire from its soil. Sinhagad fort, Shaniwar Wada, Raigad — history is never more than a short drive away.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pune-glance-item">
          <span class="pg-emoji">🎓</span>
          <strong><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Oxford of the East">पूर्वेचे ऑक्सफर्ड</span></strong>
          <p>Pune has been India's education capital for over a century. Home to Savitribai Phule Pune University, IIT Pune, IISER, FTII, and over 800 colleges — it thinks deeply and builds seriously.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pune-glance-item">
          <span class="pg-emoji">🎭</span>
          <strong><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Cultural Capital">सांस्कृतिक राजधानी</span></strong>
          <p>Classical music, Marathi theatre (<span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Marathi theater / drama">नाटक</span>), literature festivals, and Ganesh utsav — Pune's cultural life runs deep. The arts here are not a weekend activity; they are the city's heartbeat.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pune-glance-item">
          <span class="pg-emoji">🍜</span>
          <strong><span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Misal · Mastani · Puran Poli">मिसळ · मस्तानी · पुरण पोळी</span></strong>
          <p>Post-monsoon October skies, 22–26°C, the Western Ghats at their greenest — and <span class="mr" lang="mr" data-en="Pune's food">पुण्याचं खाणं</span> that will outlast any conference talk in your memory.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

